---
title: The blog
teaser: "Thoughts, lessons learned, and the occasional web oddity."
layout: layouts/base.njk
pagination:
  data: collections.blogPosts
  size: 15
  alias: pagedPosts
permalink: "/blog/{% if pagination.pageNumber > 0 %}{{ pagination.pageNumber + 1 }}/{% endif %}"
---
{%- set isFirstPage = pagination.pageNumber == 0 -%}
{%- set glance = corpusStats.blogPosts -%}
<section>
  <h1 class="kh-font-headline kh-font-headline--display kh-text-heading--1">{{title}}</h1>

  {%- if isFirstPage %}
  {#- Framing before the list. A bare reverse-chronological feed answers
      "what's newest" and nothing else; a reader arriving cold has no way to
      tell what the writing is for or whether it is still going. -#}
  <div class="kh-content">
    <p>Notes from building and running public-facing digital systems inside
    complex organizations: platform and content architecture, design systems,
    measurement that survives contact with reality, and how AI is changing
    the work rather than replacing it. Some posts are worked-through
    arguments; some are a fix I did not want to look up twice.</p>
    <p>Written for practitioners. Nothing here is sponsored, and nothing is
    written to a publishing schedule &mdash; the rhythm below is what it is.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="kh-section-head kh-u-margin__top--1200">
    <h2 id="start-here" class="kh-text-heading--2"><span class="kh-section-number">1.0</span>Start here</h2>
    <span class="kh-meta">Picked, not ranked</span>
  </div>
  <div class="kh-content">
    <p>If you only read a few, read these.</p>
  </div>
  {% include "partials/picked.njk" %}

  <div class="kh-section-head kh-u-margin__top--1200">
    <h2 id="pace" class="kh-text-heading--2"><span class="kh-section-number">2.0</span>Pace &amp; scale</h2>
    <span class="kh-meta">Counted at build time</span>
  </div>
  {%- set glanceLabel = "blog posts" %}
  {% include "partials/register-glance.njk" %}

  <div class="kh-section-head kh-u-margin__top--1200">
    <h2 id="subjects" class="kh-text-heading--2"><span class="kh-section-number">3.0</span>Recurring subjects</h2>
    <span class="kh-meta">{{ collections.topics | length }} topics in all</span>
  </div>
  <div class="kh-content">
    <p>The ones that come back most often. <a href="/directory/#subjects">The full index</a>
    has the rest, with how each has risen and fallen by year.</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="kh-topic-chips">
    {%- for t in collections.topics | limitItems(8) %}
    <li class="kh-topic-chips__item">
      <a class="kh-topic-chips__link" href="/topics/{{ t.slug }}/">{{ t.topic }}</a>
      <span class="kh-topic-chips__count">{{ t.count }}</span>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  {%- endif %}

  <div class="kh-section-head kh-u-margin__top--1200">
    <h2 id="posts" class="kh-text-heading--2"><span class="kh-section-number">{% if isFirstPage %}4.0{% else %}1.0{% endif %}</span>All posts</h2>
    <span class="kh-meta">Newest first{% if not isFirstPage %} &middot; page {{ pagination.pageNumber + 1 }}{% endif %}</span>
  </div>
  {% include "partials/search-box.njk" %}

  {#- The entry list is other entries' titles and teasers, so it is chrome by
      the CLAUDE.md rule -- the same marker topic pages and the archive already
      carry. Without it a search for "drupal" returned "All writing" (pages
      /all/4/ and /all/5/) as results, competing with the articles themselves.
      The page's own intro stays indexed, so it is still findable as a page. -#}
  <div class="kh-datasheet-list" data-pagefind-ignore>
  {%- for post in pagedPosts -%}
    {% include "partials/post-summary.njk" %}
  {%- endfor -%}
  </div>

  {% set pagerLabel = "Blog pagination" %}
  {% set pagerNewer = "Newer posts" %}
  {% set pagerOlder = "Older posts" %}
  {% include "partials/pager.njk" %}
</section>
